\,$ which is considered a special (trivial) subspace of ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. The origin $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ lies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-158100/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a8dbbab-2dea-5fff-86f0-3411f5405ee9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158100"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
